1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,320
(The Underworld)

2
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:12,080
(Shen Yanlin)

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,940
♪Cruel world, where trust runs thin♪
(Ling Che)

4
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,320
♪Blades clash. Who will rise above?♪
(Shuangdao Hui)

5
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:28,040
♪Behind every smile, danger waits♪
(Dongshan Tai)

6
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:30,520
(Fei Liu)

7
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:35,080
♪Know your limits, know your worth♪
(Luo Song)

8
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:39,800
♪Stand strong against the raging tide♪
(Annie)

9
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:44,120
♪Ask how many times I've lost my way♪

10
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:49,000
♪Storms rage on the road to power♪

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,960
♪Let old promises fade into memory♪

12
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:58,040
♪Alone and fearless, I won't back down♪

13
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:02,120
♪Power is a crown forged in blood♪

14
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:09,040
♪Brotherhood is shelter from the storm♪

15
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:15,680
=The Underworld=

16
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:18,800
=Episode 23=

17
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:48,599
Just a little something.

18
00:01:49,239 --> 00:01:49,920
About the development project,

19
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:51,040
I really owe you one.

20
00:01:51,519 --> 00:01:53,159
I'll be counting on you in the future.

21
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:54,880
(Loyalty)

22
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:58,640
You're too kind, Mr. Men.

23
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,040
There's only so much money

24
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,319
one man can make.

25
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:06,319
Helping everyone make money

26
00:02:07,079 --> 00:02:08,439
is part of my job as a shot-caller.

27
00:02:10,919 --> 00:02:11,759
Lin.

28
00:02:12,719 --> 00:02:13,479
About what happened before,

29
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:14,800
I...

30
00:02:15,639 --> 00:02:16,599
didn't really have a choice.

31
00:02:17,479 --> 00:02:18,120
Before?

32
00:02:18,879 --> 00:02:19,719
What happened before?

33
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,800
No hard feelings, alright?

34
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:29,120
I'm meeting some officials
from the Investment Bureau,

35
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,719
so I won't keep you elders.

36
00:02:34,759 --> 00:02:36,960
We'll get going, then.

37
00:02:41,599 --> 00:02:42,280
See you.

38
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:49,479
Boss Lin, you're really letting
Mai Gao off?

39
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:53,599
Some things

40
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:56,120
still need someone to do them.

41
00:02:57,040 --> 00:03:00,000
(Shicheng Xingwan Bank Loan Agreement)

42
00:03:11,919 --> 00:03:12,520
(Lin,)

43
00:03:13,159 --> 00:03:14,400
(the bank loan)

44
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:15,280
(has been approved.)

45
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:18,599
(So now,)

46
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,319
(the shantytown project)

47
00:03:20,599 --> 00:03:22,599
(can finally get underway.)

48
00:04:33,879 --> 00:04:34,639
Officer Lin.

49
00:04:35,399 --> 00:04:36,279
Miss me?

50
00:04:44,279 --> 00:04:44,920
Got a new car?

51
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:50,399
Nice ride.

52
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,639
Put on that uniform,

53
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,160
and suddenly you're
not one of us anymore.

54
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:00,920
Boss Che.

55
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:05,839
You sure have a lot of "bosses".

56
00:05:08,399 --> 00:05:09,879
W-Working this hard.

57
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,560
Out here in the sun, Officer.

58
00:05:12,079 --> 00:05:13,360
Do they at least pay you overtime?

59
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:17,519
Officer Lin.

60
00:05:19,199 --> 00:05:20,160
My car's parked over there.

61
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:22,199
Go ahead and ticket me.

62
00:05:25,439 --> 00:05:26,240
He's mute.

63
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:28,480
Show him some charity.

64
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:31,759
Sir.

65
00:05:31,879 --> 00:05:32,680
Is that enough?

66
00:05:33,279 --> 00:05:33,879
Enough?

67
00:05:34,519 --> 00:05:35,399
Sir.

68
00:05:35,879 --> 00:05:37,120
Throwing money around isn't illegal,
is it?

69
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:00,800
Move back.

70
00:06:02,519 --> 00:06:04,240
Everyone, step back. Make some room.

71
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:06,920
Back up. Back up.

72
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,920
(Headquarters, we found a body
under the Rongxing Road Bridge.)

73
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:16,120
(The victim appears to have died
of a drug overdose.)

74
00:06:28,079 --> 00:06:28,720
Coming through.

75
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:32,240
What unit are you with?

76
00:06:37,319 --> 00:06:37,920
Thanks for your work.

77
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:39,279
I'll take it from here.

78
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:01,800
Bobo.

79
00:07:02,879 --> 00:07:04,240
Who was the guy in charge today?

80
00:07:04,879 --> 00:07:06,680
That's Cheng, head
of the Criminal Division.

81
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:07,839
Cheng?

82
00:07:12,199 --> 00:07:12,680
Want some?

83
00:07:15,839 --> 00:07:16,959
He's pretty handsome, isn't he?

84
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:18,680
If I remember right,

85
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,879
he's about your age.

86
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:23,240
You two couldn't have been more than
a few classes apart.

87
00:07:25,079 --> 00:07:27,439
Are you jealous because I called him
handsome?

88
00:07:31,879 --> 00:07:32,680
Yeah.

89
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,480
(Police Records)

90
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:13,720
(Victim Information)

91
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:17,080
(Signature: Wang Cheng
Signature: Luo Song)

92
00:09:17,679 --> 00:09:18,360
Wang Cheng.

93
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:22,159
Cheng...

94
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,800
(Signature: Wang Cheng
Signature: Luo Song)

95
00:09:34,159 --> 00:09:36,159
How are you settling into the job?

96
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:41,919
Officer Luo.

97
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:46,879
I don't want to keep doing support work
at the station.

98
00:09:47,759 --> 00:09:49,799
I want to start working major cases
as soon as possible.

99
00:09:50,639 --> 00:09:52,080
Can I transfer to the Criminal Division?

100
00:09:54,159 --> 00:09:55,440
I understand how you feel.

101
00:09:56,639 --> 00:09:59,639
Every cop wants to work the big cases.

102
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:01,679
The local station

103
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,639
may not handle many serious crimes,

104
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:04,559
but

105
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:07,279
the work here is still essential.

106
00:10:07,679 --> 00:10:08,360
I understand.

107
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:11,279
But I can't help feeling useless here.

108
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,559
Don't think of it that way.

109
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:15,279
The work we do here

110
00:10:15,279 --> 00:10:17,360
directly affects people's
everyday lives.

111
00:10:17,919 --> 00:10:18,799
If we do it right,

112
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,080
we can stop crimes before they happen.

113
00:10:22,759 --> 00:10:23,279
Got it.

114
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:34,759
Here are all the stolen-vehicle files.

115
00:10:35,679 --> 00:10:36,200
Thanks.

116
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:39,000
These cases are all closed.

117
00:10:39,159 --> 00:10:40,240
Why are you looking through them?

118
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,000
I still have

119
00:10:44,279 --> 00:10:45,120
other cases.

120
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,879
And I haven't written the closing report
for the chief yet.

121
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:49,039
I want to look these over
and see how to write them.

122
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:50,240
Okay.

123
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:15,600
(Vehicle Information:
Make/Model; License Plate)

124
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:29,720
(Shatina, 28 Maikun Road)

125
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:34,200
Officer,

126
00:11:34,919 --> 00:11:36,120
I've already told you

127
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,960
every bad thing I've ever done

128
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:39,720
since I was old enough to remember.

129
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,720
I really didn't steal that car.

130
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:43,200
I... I swear!

131
00:11:45,879 --> 00:11:47,080
Please, just let me go.

132
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:49,200
It really wasn't me.

133
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,799
(Liu'an Driving School)
Why don't you just beat me up

134
00:11:50,799 --> 00:11:51,639
if it'll make you feel better?

135
00:11:54,919 --> 00:11:55,840
Don't go!

136
00:12:04,759 --> 00:12:05,919
Headquarters says

137
00:12:05,919 --> 00:12:07,960
they're modernizing the whole system.

138
00:12:08,840 --> 00:12:09,879
All these files

139
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,399
have to be entered
into the computer tonight.

140
00:12:14,039 --> 00:12:14,720
All of them?

141
00:12:19,879 --> 00:12:21,519
This thing's a real pain.

142
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:24,000
You need the chief's login
to enter everything.

143
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,840
I know a little about computers.

144
00:12:31,519 --> 00:12:32,840
I type a little slowly,

145
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:35,159
but I can get all this done tonight.

146
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:37,440
I couldn't ask you to do that.

147
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:40,519
I'm on duty tonight anyway.

148
00:12:41,759 --> 00:12:42,200
Thanks.

149
00:12:42,519 --> 00:12:43,559
Egg tarts are on me next time.

150
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:55,120
(Badge No. 01789
Password: SU1294)

151
00:13:11,519 --> 00:13:12,080
Lin.

152
00:13:12,679 --> 00:13:15,039
You handled the bank matter very well.

153
00:13:25,759 --> 00:13:28,480
Once the relocation money goes
through the right channels,

154
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:30,120
no one can touch us.

155
00:13:31,679 --> 00:13:33,600
From now on, every dollar
that goes into our pockets

156
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,399
will be clean.

157
00:13:35,639 --> 00:13:36,519
There's something

158
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:38,039
I need you to do.

159
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:40,080
What is it?

160
00:13:41,039 --> 00:13:42,120
A friend of mine

161
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:44,159
accidentally killed a dancer.

162
00:13:45,759 --> 00:13:47,480
A dancer's life isn't worth much,

163
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:49,480
but this friend of mine

164
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,159
was just transferred

165
00:13:51,679 --> 00:13:52,399
and more or less

166
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:54,240
promoted.

167
00:13:55,679 --> 00:13:58,519
Something like this could jeopardize
his position.

168
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:00,159
I need you to find

169
00:14:00,879 --> 00:14:02,720
one of your most trusted brothers

170
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:04,399
to take the fall.

171
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:05,919
Mr. Wan,

172
00:14:07,159 --> 00:14:08,320
I'm not sure what you mean.

173
00:14:09,679 --> 00:14:11,240
I don't trust just anyone.

174
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:15,360
If you want to stay my friend,

175
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:17,919
you'll have to show me some loyalty.

176
00:14:20,879 --> 00:14:21,679
Mr. Wan,

177
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:25,039
in our world, loyalty means everything.

178
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,600
If I make one of my brothers
take the blame,

179
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,759
I'm afraid

180
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:32,240
my men won't respect me anymore.

181
00:14:38,279 --> 00:14:39,960
Don't tell me you actually think

182
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:42,559
just because you've got a seat
at the table,

183
00:14:43,159 --> 00:14:44,919
you can stand

184
00:14:45,559 --> 00:14:46,799
as an equal to someone like me.

185
00:14:47,159 --> 00:14:47,960
Mr. Wan,

186
00:14:48,639 --> 00:14:49,639
what you're asking,

187
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:51,240
I can't do it.

188
00:14:53,159 --> 00:14:54,759
Use that useless brain of yours

189
00:14:54,759 --> 00:14:55,960
and think carefully.

190
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:58,720
Why do you think the police
haven't touched you?

191
00:14:59,720 --> 00:15:00,399
You really think

192
00:15:01,279 --> 00:15:02,559
it's because they have no evidence?

193
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:16,720
Without my backing,

194
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,120
you really think you could've

195
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:20,679
taken the shot-caller seat that easily?

196
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:24,120
If you don't want to keep that seat,

197
00:15:25,679 --> 00:15:28,039
I've got plenty of people
who can replace you.

198
00:15:29,039 --> 00:15:30,240
You're not the only dog

199
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:33,559
at my heel.

200
00:15:44,399 --> 00:15:45,039
Mr. Wan.

201
00:15:46,879 --> 00:15:47,960
What you asked for,

202
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,480
I'll take care of it.

203
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:30,040
♪They tell me not to walk head bowed♪

204
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:36,040
♪They say look up to see the light♪

205
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:42,280
♪I don't know what the light looks like♪

206
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:46,440
♪All I know is the mud feels cold♪

207
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:56,560
♪I used to believe I could
grit my teeth and make it through♪

208
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:02,880
♪That if I endured it,
I'd come out whole♪

209
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:08,360
♪But every morning,
when I look in the mirror♪

210
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:11,120
♪The same face is still staring back
at me♪

211
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:13,400
♪Stray dog, stray dog♪

212
00:17:15,520 --> 00:17:17,240
♪Stray dog, stray dog♪

213
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:20,080
♪I want to hold my head up too♪

214
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:25,720
♪But this life won't let me go♪

215
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:29,600
♪Stray dog, stray dog♪

216
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:42,000
♪Stray dog, stray dog♪
